wer.type/text} :answer/value "insufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170667} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170668}] :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170666}] :question/math-academy-id "q-252047" :question/problem "A company claims that the amounts of coffee dispensed by its coffee machine are normally distributed with variance $σ^{2} = 3ml^{2}$. After routine maintenance, the owner of the coffee machine hopes that the machine has become more consistent. He decides to conduct a hypothesis test at the $10%$ significance level.\n\nThe owner of the coffee machine collected data from $19$ cups of coffee after the maintenance and found an unbiased estimate for the population variance was $s^{2} = 2.5ml^{2}$.\n\nThe table below shows the values $χ_{ν, p}$ such that $P(X > χ_{ν, p}) = p$ for some particular values of $ν$ and $p$, where $X$ follows a chi-square distribution $χ^{2}(ν)$ with $ν$ degrees of freedom.\n\n| $ν∖p$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ | $0.800$ | $0.200$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $18$ | $9.390$ | $10.865$ | $12.857$ | $22.760$ | $25.989$ | $28.869$ |\n| $19$ | $10.117$ | $11.651$ | $13.716$ | $23.900$ | $27.204$ | $30.144$ |\n| $20$ | $10.851$ | $12.443$ | $14.578$ | $25.038$ | $28.412$ | $31.410$ |\n\nUsing this information, select the options that make the following statements true.\n\nThe test statistic for this test is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nAt the $10%$ level of significance, there is\n{{field-2}}\nevidence that $σ^{2} < 3ml^{2}$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170670} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "insufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170671}